[ti:Day 01]

[00:00.00]chamber [ˈtʃeɪmbə(r)]n. 会议室，会议厅；商会，会所 a. 秘密的 例 He took his seat in an unobserved corner of the chamber.
[00:10.44]complexion [kəmˈplekʃn]n. 情况；局面 例 If the fiscal risks can't be prevented efficiently, the tragedy complexion would result, and the social system and economic order should be restructured. 搭 put a different complexion on sth. 改变…的 局面
[00:34.08]compress [kəmˈpres]v. 压缩；浓缩 例 My goal with time management is to effectively compress, organise and prioritise activities for maximum efficiency.
[00:49.20]resourceful [rɪˈsɔːsfl]a. 资源丰富的；足智多谋的 例 She is a clever and resourceful manager.
[00:57.60]expertise [ˌekspɜːˈtiːz]n. 专门技术，专门知识；专家的意 见 例 The business consultant that we really need is someone who can offer expertise in business logic. 搭 expertise in 在…方面的专业技能
[01:14.88]advent [ˈædvent]n. (尤指不寻常的人或事物的)到来，出 现 例 People's lives were greatly changed by the advent of computers. 搭 advent of... …的出现
[01:27.60]wildcat [ˈwaɪldkæt]a. 高风险的；靠不住的；非法经营的
[01:31.80]thesis [ˈθiːsɪs]n. 论题，命题；论点；论文
[01:35.16]robust [rəʊˈbʌst]a. 强健的，结实的；坚固的；浓烈的， 醇厚的 搭 robust coffee 浓咖啡
[01:41.52]irrevocable [ɪˈrevəkəbl]a. 不可撤销的；不可废止的；不能改 变的
[01:46.56]mull [mʌl]v. 思索，思考 例 As you mull all these things over, inspiration will strike you. 搭 mull sth. over 仔细考虑某事
[01:57.24]wrongheaded [ˌrɒŋˈhedɪd]a. 固执的；坚持错误的 例 The proposal to develop a new market in the small city was proven to be a wholly wrongheaded idea.
[02:11.04]cultivate [ˈkʌltɪveɪt]vt. 耕作，栽培；养殖；培养；陶冶； 发展 例 To increase the income of farmers in our country, we should encourage them to cultivate this new variety of rice. 搭 cultivate sb.'s interest in sth. 培养某人在某 事方面的兴趣 / cultivate sb.'s musical taste 陶 冶某人的音乐品味
[02:36.60]wrapping [ˈræpɪŋ]n. 包装纸；包装材料 a. 包装用的
[02:40.44]safeguard [ˈseɪfɡɑːd]n. 防护措施；防护装置；保障条款 vt. 防护；捍卫 例 The union has taken measures to safeguard the interests of its members.
[02:53.04]fruitful [ˈfruːtfl]a. 有收获的，富有成效的；多产的 例 The work will be more fruitful under this program. 搭 fruitful plan 富有成效的计划
[03:04.68]menace [ˈmenəs]n. 具有危险性的人(或物)；威胁，威吓 vt. 威胁，威吓 例 The careless staff are a menace to a whole team.
[03:14.40]comprehensive [ˌkɒmprɪˈhensɪv]a. 全面的；详尽的；综合的；有 理解力的 例 This discovery prompted consumer groups, as well as scientists, to push for comprehensive testing of the potential allergenicity of GM foods.
[03:34.80]profligacy [ˈprɒflɪɡəsi]a. 不检点的；挥霍无度的 n. 浪子； 恣意挥霍(的人)；浪费
[03:40.92]technique [tekˈniːk]n. 工艺，技术；方法；技巧，手艺
[03:45.12]loan [ləʊn]n. 贷款；借款；借用 vt. 借，借给 vi. 借出 例 If we could get a loan, the company would keep going. 搭 on loan 借用；借调
[03:55.68]cannibalise [ˈkænɪbəlaɪz]v. 拆用配件；抽调人员 例 It becomes necessary to cannibalise unsuccessful projects to fund those which can proceed.
[04:09.36]confine [kənˈfaɪn]vt. 限制；使局限；监禁 n. 边界；疆界 例 Please confine your remarks to the subject we are debating. 搭 confine oneself to 只涉及，只限于
[04:22.68]destination [ˌdestɪˈneɪʃn]n. 目的地，终点；目标
[04:27.00]protocol [ˈprəʊtəkɒl]n. 草案；协议，议定书；礼仪
[04:31.08]proforma [ˌprəʊˈfɔːmə]a. 形式上的；预计的 n. 形式发票； 估价单；预计报表
[04:36.60]raft [rɑːft]n. 木筏；救生筏；大量 vt. 用筏子运送 vi. 乘筏子(渡河) 搭 a raft of 大量 / life raft 救生筏
[04:44.04]deteriorate [dɪˈtɪəriəreɪt]v. 恶化，变坏 例 Working conditions in the factory continue to deteriorate. 搭 deteriorate into 恶化成 / deteriorate the quality of the air 破坏空气质量
[05:00.84]backup [ˈbækʌp]n. 备份；复写 vt. 做备份 a. 候补的；应 急的 例 The backup system is an essential part of your work.
[05:10.44]banknote [ˈbæŋknəʊt]n. 银行券；钞票 例 At present, the banking system does not have enough banknotes to meet all the residents' requests. 搭 banknote paper 纸币用纸
[05:25.92]ally [əˈlaɪ]v. 结盟；联合 [ˈælaɪ]n. 同盟国；同盟者 例 Common interests allied these two banks with each other. 搭 ally (oneself) with sb./sth. 与…结盟
[05:39.48]watermark [ˈwɔːtəmɑːk]n. 水印；水位标记
[05:43.08]mission [ˈmɪʃn]n. 任务，使命；代表团，使团 搭 carry out one's mission 执行任务
[05:49.44]commission [kəˈmɪʃn]n. 委员会；委任；授权；代理；代理 费，佣金 vt. 委任；授权 例 The report was submitted to the commission for its consideration. 搭 in commission 在使用中，可使用 / on commission 提取佣金地 / out of commission 不能使用，已损坏
[06:09.60]acquiesce [ˌækwiˈes]vi. 默许；默认 例 The department manager acquiesced in his demand for a higher salary. 搭 acquiesce in/to 默认
[06:21.96]readjust [ˌriːəˈdʒʌst]vt. 使再调整；使重新适应
[06:26.04]stock [stɒk]n. 证券，股票；存货，库存
[06:28.92]convert [kənˈvɜːt]vt. 转化，转变；兑换 例 Another approach is to suppress anger and then convert it.
[06:38.28]differential [ˌdɪfəˈrenʃl]a. 差别的 n. (同一行业中熟练工人和 非熟练工人的)工资差别
[06:44.76]periodical [ˌpɪəriˈɒdɪkl]a. 周期的；定期的 n. 期刊；杂志
[06:49.56]cartel [kɑːˈtel]n. 卡特尔；同业联合；联合企业 例 The cartel exists to protect its members from market retribution.
[07:00.00]spectator [spekˈteɪtə(r)]n. 观众，旁观者
[07:03.84]trawl [trɔːl]n. 拖网；排钩绳 v. 用拖网捕(鱼) 搭 trawl board 拖网板
[07:09.00]valid [ˈvælɪd]a. 有效的；具有法律效力的；正当的；有 根据的 例 The building lease is valid for six months.
[07:17.64]temp [temp]n. 临时雇员；替班
[07:19.92]overpay [ˌəʊvəˈpeɪ]v. 多付(钱财) 例 I am worried that the government will overpay the shareholders at the banks.
[07:30.84]emphasis [ˈemfəsɪs]n. 强调；重点 例 We should lay enough emphasis on the needs and demands of current customers. 搭 lay emphasis on/upon sth. 把重点放在…上
[07:45.24]corner [kɔːnə(r)]vt. 垄断；把…逼入困境 vi. 囤积 n. 囤 积；垄断；角落 例 They saw the great opportunity to corner the market and earned a lot of money. 搭 drive sb. into a corner 把某人逼得走投无路 / in the corner 秘密地 / make a corner in sth. 囤 积某物
[08:06.12]miscellaneous [ˌmɪsəˈleɪniəs]a. 混杂的；多方面的；多才多艺的
[08:11.40]costume [ˈkɒstjuːm]n. 服装 例 The costume advertisements in Paris broadened his outlook. 搭 costume ball 化装舞会 / costume book 时装 画册 / costume designer 服装设计师 / costume play 古装戏
[08:28.44]luminary [ˈluːmɪnəri]n. 发光体；名人；杰出人物
[08:32.40]capitalise [ˈkæpɪtəlaɪz]vt. 用大写字母书写；为…提供资 金；使转化成资本；从…中获利 vi. 利用；积累资 本 例 The firm is seeking to capitalise on technological innovations, reduce costs and become strongly competitive. 搭 capitalise on 充分利用；从…中获利；投机倒 把
[08:54.84]resilient [rɪˈzɪliənt]a. 有弹性的；有回弹力的
[08:58.80]probe [prəʊb]v. 探查；探究；查找 例 He has been probing for the information relevant to business management.
[09:09.00]subsequent [ˈsʌbsɪkwənt]a. 随后的，后来的 搭 be subsequent to 在…之后
[09:15.12]obligate [ˈɒblɪɡeɪt]vt. 使在法律上(或道义上)负有责任； (在法律上)强迫 a. 有责任的，有义务的 例 The current accounting rules do not obligate companies to report their estimated retiree benefit expenses. 搭 be obligate to do sth. 有责任做某事
[09:36.12]continent [ˈkɒntɪnənt]n. 洲，大陆 a. 自制的，克制的 例 Natural disasters have obviously contributed to the continent's economic crisis.
[09:49.08]vindicate [ˈvɪndɪkeɪt]vt. 维护；辩护；证明…无辜；证明… 合理 例 The decision to develop new products was vindicated when the sales increased greatly.
[10:02.88]complex [ˈkɒmpleks]n. 联合企业；综合体 a. 由多部分组 成的；复合的；复杂的 例 Those same companies are investing heavily to create a cyber-industrial complex.
[10:16.80]machinery [məˈʃiːnəri]n. 机械；机器；机械装置；机构
[10:21.12]mobilise [ˈməʊbəlaɪz]vt. 动员；调动；鼓动；使流通 例 No power can any longer mobilise its armed forces in secret.
[10:31.44]conservative [kənˈsɜːvətɪv]a. 能保存的；保险的；保守的；谨 慎的；(式样等)不时新的 n. 保守的人 例 At a conservative estimate, the company will be earning up to 1 billion dollars this year.
[10:47.76]dollar-denominated [ˌdɒlə(r)dɪˈnɒmɪneɪtɪd]a. 以美元计价的 例 In order to prevent devaluation of their dollars, they have no option but to keep buying yet more dollar-denominated securities.
[11:06.84]subliminal [ˌsʌbˈlɪmɪnl]a. 潜意识的
[11:10.32]monotony [məˈnɒtəni]n. 单调；千篇一律 例 To avoid monotony, we must always find something innovative.
[11:20.04]adjacent [əˈdʒeɪsnt]a. 邻近的；毗连的 例 He despised the six colleagues at the adjacent table. 搭 adjacent to 与…毗连
[11:30.72]illuminate [ɪˈluːmɪneɪt]vt. 照明，照亮；阐明，启发；说明 vi. 照亮；用灯装饰 例 Doing so can make it easier to illuminate several important aspects of consumer behaviour.
[11:46.08]mint [mɪnt]n. 薄荷；造币厂；巨额，大量 vt. 铸造(硬 币)；创造 例 I have a friend working in the German Mint.
[11:54.72]fraught [frɔːt]a. 担心的，忧虑的；充满的；伴随着的 例 The security situation has indeed been fraught with peril. 搭 fraught with 充满，伴随着
[12:06.84]enact [ɪˈnækt]vt. 颁布(法令)；制定(法律) 例 The new law is enacted by the government to regulate the market.
[12:16.80]update [ˌʌpˈdeɪt]v. 更新；使现代化；校正，修正
[12:20.52]leviathan [ləˈvaɪəθən]n. 海中怪兽；庞然大物 a. 极大的； 强大的 例 It's truly lucky that democracy survived the Civil War with the developing industrial leviathan.
[12:35.52]correspondence [ˌkɒrəˈspɒndəns]n. 信件；通信，联系；符合， 一致；相似 例 Our correspondence is limited to a few commercial letters. 搭 correspondence school 函授学校
[12:50.52]alienate [ˈeɪliəneɪt]vt. 使疏远，离间；转让，让渡(财产 等)；使转移 例 The old gentleman was determined to alienate all of his property to charity upon his decease. 搭 alienate from 疏远
[13:07.08]overvalued [ˌəʊvəˈvæljuːd]a. 定价过高的；估价过高的
[13:11.64]attorney [əˈtɜːni]n. 律师；代理人 例 For more information about setting up a business, contact a qualified attorney.
[13:22.92]exclusion [ɪkˈskluːʒn]n. 排斥，排除；被排除在外的事物 搭 to the exclusion of 排除掉，排斥
[13:30.12]cargo [ˈkɑːɡəʊ]n. (船、飞机等载走的)货物；货运；一 批，一堆 例 The crew lashed down the cargo on the fore deck. 搭 a cargo of 一批；一船
[13:41.04]dispense [dɪˈspens]vt. 分配，分发；施行 例 The host required the experts to dispense with their prepared speeches and enter directly into discussion. 搭 dispense with 免除，省去
[13:57.72]dissipate [ˈdɪsɪpeɪt]vi. 消散，消失 vt. 使消散，使消失；浪 费 例 The pace of domestic economic recovery would slow down because the effects of rebuilding stocks overseas will dissipate eventually.
[14:16.32]cynical [ˈsɪnɪkl]a. 怀疑的；愤世嫉俗的；冷嘲热讽的 例 The enormous difficulty makes him cynical
[14:24.72]specification [ˌspesɪfɪˈkeɪʃn]n. 详述；明细单；说明书；[pl.] 规格 搭 fall short of specifications 不符合规格 / up to specifications 符合规格
